          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, the case concerns whether a Miranda warning given before a second statement removes the presumption that an earlier unwarned statement taints the later confession."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-303372bb99f1-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 52,
              "start": 52
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court is asked to determine whether the failure to give a Miranda warning for the first statement renders that statement involuntary and therefore capable of tainting the second statement."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
